\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces $\log \,\mathrm  {IPR}$ vs $\log N$ for the mid-gap eigenstate of the Fibonacci (blue circles) and tribonacci (red squares) chains at their respective natural iteration lengths. Solid lines are OLS fits; shaded bands show the $1\sigma $ uncertainty interval. The tribonacci IPR sequence is monotone after excluding compact defect states (see text); the resulting $D_{2,\mathrm  {trib}} = 0.282$ is significantly below $D_{2,\mathrm  {fib}} = 0.646$, confirming stronger multifractality.}}{12}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:d2natural}{{6}{12}{$\log \,\mathrm {IPR}$ vs $\log N$ for the mid-gap eigenstate of the Fibonacci (blue circles) and tribonacci (red squares) chains at their respective natural iteration lengths. Solid lines are OLS fits; shaded bands show the $1\sigma $ uncertainty interval. The tribonacci IPR sequence is monotone after excluding compact defect states (see text); the resulting $D_{2,\mathrm {trib}} = 0.282$ is significantly below $D_{2,\mathrm {fib}} = 0.646$, confirming stronger multifractality}{figure.caption.9}{}}
